      "text": "# Community Garden Operating Agreement & Management Plan\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nThis document establishes a transparent, inclusive, and financially sustainable framework for the community garden. It addresses the current resource constraints (30 plots for 40 households + 10 waitlisted), financial deficits, and social conflicts. The core philosophy is **\"Equity over Equality,\"** ensuring that physical ability, financial status, and time availability do not prevent participation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Inclusive Operating Agreement\n\n### Article I: Membership & Allocation\n**Clause 1.1: Eligibility & Definition of Household**\nA \"Household\" is defined as a single residential unit. One plot is allocated per household. Subletting or sharing a plot between households is prohibited to ensure fair access.\n\n**Clause 1.2: Transparent Allocation Process**\nTo address the council\u2019s request for transparency, plots are allocated via a **Weighted Lottery System** rather than \"first-come, first-served.\"\n*   **Step 1:** All applicants (current members and waitlisted) submit a registration form.\n*   **Step 2:** Points are assigned based on:\n    *   10 points: New applicant (no prior plot).\n    *   5 points: Applicant who has been on the waitlist for >1 year.\n    *   3 points: Applicant with a documented accessibility need (see Article III).\n    *   1 point: Applicant who has volunteered in the past year.\n*   **Step 3:** A random lottery is drawn from the pool, weighted by points.\n*   **Step 4:** Results are published publicly with anonymized IDs to ensure auditability.\n\n**Clause 1.3: Fair Waitlist Handling**\n*   **Waitlist Cap:** The waitlist is capped at 20 households to prevent indefinite waiting.\n*   **Rotation Policy:** Households on the waitlist for more than 24 months without receiving a plot are offered a \"Community Volunteer Role\" (see Article III) which grants priority status for the next lottery.\n*   **Vacancy Notification:** When a plot becomes vacant, the next household in the weighted lottery queue is notified within 48 hours. They have 7 days to accept or forfeit their spot to the next candidate.\n\n### Article II: Plot Usage & Conduct\n**Clause 2.1: Prohibited Structures**\nPermanent structures (sheds, greenhouses, raised beds fixed to the ground) are banned per lease terms.\n*   **Allowed:** Portable containers, temporary hoop houses (removed in winter), and movable trellises.\n*   **Enforcement:** Structures left over 14 days after a notice are removed by the Committee at the owner\u2019s expense.\n\n**Clause 2.2: Chemical & Organic Standards**\n*   **Ban on Synthetic Pesticides/Herbicides:** To address complaints about chemical sprays, only OMRI-listed (Organic Materials Review Institute) products are permitted.\n*   **Buffer Zones:** A 1-meter buffer zone must be maintained between plots to prevent drift.\n*   **Complaint Protocol:** If a neighbor suspects chemical use, they must report it to the Garden Committee. The accused must provide product labels. First offense: Warning. Second offense: Loss of plot for one season.\n\n**Clause 2.3: Shade & Light Management**\n*   **Height Limits:** No plant or structure may exceed 6 feet in height if it casts shade on a neighboring plot between 10:00 AM and 2:00 PM.\n*   **Tall Plant Placement:** Tall crops (corn, sunflowers) must be planted on the north side of the plot (in the Northern Hemisphere) to minimize shading of neighbors.\n\n**Clause 2.4: Unattended Produce**\n*   **Harvest Window:** Produce must be harvested within 7 days of ripening.\n*   **Abandonment:** Unharvested produce left for >7 days may be harvested by any member. This addresses complaints about waste and encourages active participation.\n\n### Article III: Accessibility & Inclusive Volunteering\n**Clause 3.1: Physical Accessibility Alternatives**\nRecognizing that some residents cannot perform physical work, the garden adopts a **\"Skills-Based Contribution\"** model.\n*   **Standard Plot:** Requires 4 hours of physical maintenance per month.\n*   **Accessible Plot (Raised Beds):** 5 plots are designated as \"Accessible Plots\" (raised to waist height, wide paths for wheelchairs). These require only 2 hours of maintenance per month.\n*   **Non-Physical Roles:** Members unable to perform physical labor may fulfill their obligation through:\n    *   **Administrative:** Managing the waitlist, drafting newsletters, or handling finances.\n    *   **Educational:** Leading workshops on composting or",
